WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.684 --> 00:00:02.987
(dramatic music)

00:00:02.987 --> 00:00:05.426
(lasso whipping)

00:00:05.426 --> 00:00:08.310
(cow mooing)

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:11.223
- [Announcer] We got one
round left, Ms. Joanna Stern.

00:00:12.201 --> 00:00:14.784
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:18.390
(grunts)

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.210
- Airpods Pro in.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.250
That's me, regretting this idea I had

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.070
to test how well these
things stay in your ears.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.120
I even had to double down on my testing

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.373
with one of New York City's
most iconic dance families.

00:00:31.661 --> 00:00:34.578
(slow opera music)

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:37.800
Why did I do this?

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.640
Well, because unlike the
$150 regular Airpods,

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.070
the $250 Airpods Pro have
active noise cancellation.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:48.960
They come with three different
size silicon rubber tips

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.310
to better fit in your ear.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.942
Plus, Airpods have been known to fall out.

00:00:52.942 --> 00:00:56.192
(dramatic opera music)

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.850
There's even a size test
that analyzes the fit

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.810
when they're in your ears and
tells you if you're all good.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.240
Heck, Apple's so confident in the fit,

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.760
they made them sweat
resistant for working out.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.390
I tested four wireless
earbuds on the bull:

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:17.290
the standard Airpods, the Airpods Pro,

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:20.870
the Samsung Galaxy buds,
and the Amazon Echo buds.

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:23.210
With each pair in, I
asked the bull operator

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:25.030
to drive at three speeds.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.419
Slow, medium, and high.

00:01:27.419 --> 00:01:28.293
Yeah.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:32.509
The regular Airpods
stayed in on all the tests

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:33.957
except for one.

00:01:38.213 --> 00:01:40.977
(buzzing)

00:01:40.977 --> 00:01:41.810
One out.

00:01:44.526 --> 00:01:45.359
Yeah.

00:01:46.891 --> 00:01:48.290
(grunting)

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:50.170
Galaxy buds in.
(dinging)

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.280
Amazon Echo buds.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.620
The Amazon Echo buds faired the worst,

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.645
falling out both times I fell.

00:01:56.645 --> 00:01:57.478
(buzzing)

00:01:57.478 --> 00:01:59.370
Amazon ear buds, oh
no, they both fell out.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.890
Amazon does include these
wing tips in the box,

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:02.890
which should help.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.390
Though, even then, they're
still the least comfortable

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:06.310
of the bunch.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:08.645
I'm not sure this was my best idea.

00:02:08.645 --> 00:02:11.370
(light classical music)

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.759
The Airpod Pros would not fall out

00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:16.710
no matter how many times I was bumped off.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.160
They just stayed securely in my ears.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.210
Didn't even really
(dinging)

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:21.043
loosen up.

00:02:23.173 --> 00:02:25.383
(dinging)
(grunting)

00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:26.216
(dinging)

00:02:26.216 --> 00:02:27.350
More good news about the Pros.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.140
If you're ever riding a mechanical bull

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.250
while trying to enjoy
some music, as one does,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.530
the Pros active noise
canceling blocked out

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.360
the machinery better than
those other competitors.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.480
Of course, that could also
mean it would block out

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.150
the sound of an oncoming train or car.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.010
That's why there's a transparency.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.360
You switch it on via the
phone or by pressing on

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.860
this little button to hear
more noises around you.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.890
Okay, so the Airpods Pros
survived the mechanical bull.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:55.883
But I had to find one
more test just to be sure.

00:02:57.137 --> 00:03:00.470
(bright woodwind music)

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:05.453
This is Tic, Tac, oh and Tay.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.780
Not only do Tic and Tac do crazy tricks,

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:11.110
but they're twins with similar ears.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:13.550
So I gave them two pairs of Airpods Pro

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.453
and well, got outta the way.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.930
Airpods are staying in.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:22.420
Again, the Airpods Pros
stayed in insanely well.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.669
Are they in?

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:24.596
- Yeah!

00:03:24.596 --> 00:03:25.520
- [Joanna] They're still in?

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.802
- Yeah.
(dinging)

00:03:27.802 --> 00:03:28.980
(dinging)
- Still stayed in.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.360
- [Joanna] We even had Tay,
another member of the family,

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.307
test them out.

00:03:34.216 --> 00:03:36.716
(light music)

00:03:38.202 --> 00:03:39.830
- Almost out.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.670
- And with that, we finally got the

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:43.822
Airpods Pro to fall out
(buzzing)

00:03:43.822 --> 00:03:45.970
with a series of clips.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.887
You're still good, so one fell out!

00:03:51.018 --> 00:03:53.685
(phone ringing)

00:03:54.993 --> 00:03:56.910
Are you (beep) kidding me?

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.250
Yes, after all of that, it turns out

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:03.490
aggressive chewing is what
can loosen up the in ear seal.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:06.763
Still, these things
stay in extremely well.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:10.583
Did it come out?

